**DEFECT 1: TestSnapshotCases.java:13,15 — ES_VERSION_6 constants have v5 values**
```java
// Line 13: public static final String ES_VERSION_6 = "5";
// Line 15: public static final String ES_VERSION_6_STANDARD_TOKEN_FILTER = "5_custom_analyzer";
```
Both `ES_VERSION_6` and `ES_VERSION_6_STANDARD_TOKEN_FILTER` are assigned v5 values (`"5"` and `"5_custom_analyzer"`). The four v6 test classes (`RestoreFromVersion6IT`, `RestoreFromVersion6CustomAnalyzerIT`, `MountFromVersion6IT`, `MountFromVersion6CustomAnalyzerIT`) all use these constants, so they will load v5 snapshot resources (`snapshot_v5_custom_analyzer.zip`) instead of the new v6 resources (`snapshot_v6_custom_analyzer.zip`). This makes the v6 tests effectively duplicates of v5 tests, providing zero v6 coverage.

**DEFECT 2: RestoreFromVersion6CustomAnalyzerIT.java:42 / MountFromVersion6CustomAnalyzerIT.java:42 — Tests assert v5 warning message for v6 snapshot**
```java
// Both files, line 42:
assertEquals("The [standard] token filter is " + "deprecated and will be removed in a future version.", warnings.getFirst());
```
Because of Defect 1, these tests actually run against the v5 snapshot (which uses `my_type` mapping), but the test class comments claim they test "ES_v6 - Custom-Analyzer" (which uses `_doc` mapping). The warning assertion may pass incidentally (same analyzer), but the test validates the wrong snapshot version — it's a false-positive v6 test.
